- Blueprint shorthand “THROTTLE | WAVE & BLADE” / “SKY & SUMMIT / OTHERS” maps to **separate** grid cells — never collapse labels.

## In-feed live alert ticker

- Floating minimalist dark toast/banner on the main Arena feed.
- Surfaces real-time open callout alerts (e.g. ⚡ `OPEN: …`) and battle accepts (e.g. 🥊 `BATTLE LIVE: …`).
- Tap deep-links into the FACEOFF hub (challenge section).

## Challenge creation & camera (1-tap)

- **`+ BATTLE` FAB** and Battles **LAUNCH ARENA CHALLENGE** → **single tap** into `UniversalCamera` challenge / opener mode (`captureOpenerOnly` / `isArenaOpenChallenge` via `MainTabs.openArenaChallenge`).
- Do **not** insert a blocking confirmation sheet before the camera.
- After opener capture, publish path may reopen Create Arena Challenge only for Publish — never block the initial camera open.
- Publish: upload opener to Supabase Storage + insert `arena_challenges` (`src/services/arenaChallengeService.js`), then **prepend** to Arena (`pushOpenChallenge`) with active **RESPOND**.

## Post-recording stability (`UniversalCamera.tsx`)

- Await native `stopRecording` / in-flight `recordAsync` **before** React state flips or navigation.
- Keep **`RECORDING_TEARDOWN_MS = 200`** (+ preview handshake) so expo-camera / expo-av release the hardware lock.
- Use `isProcessing` / `isFinalizingClip` gates; clear preview players and recording refs on unmount / `safeNavigateHome`.
- Do not remount/unmount `CameraView` mid-flush.

## Scalability vision (do not regress when adding)

- Main card remains the primary 1v1 comparison.
- Future: expandable horizontal **Responses Tray** of mini split-screen thumbnails to swap active challengers into full clarity — add alongside this chrome, do not replace the dual-pane card or RESPOND CTA.

## Re-hydration prompt (maintain)

Load project context for BAWAAL: Keep the main Arena surface as a single clutter-free video feed with ARENA + FACEOFF in the header. FACEOFF hosts scores ticker, sports category grid, and open callouts. Preserve the in-feed floating alert ticker that deep-links into FACEOFF. Keep the 1-tap challenge creation route to `UniversalCamera.tsx` active, preserving the asynchronous video teardown delay (200ms) to prevent native camera memory unmount crashes.

